  <h1 class="page-title">Service Model & Commercial Terms</h1>
  <p class="page-hero__lead">Five steps from account opening to follow-up — with written answers to the questions every procurement officer asks before opening an account.</p>
  
</div></div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  
<div class="sec-head">
  <span class="eyebrow"><i></i>The service model for clinics</span>
  <h2 class="sec-title">Step by step</h2>
  
</div>
  <div class="grid grid-5" style="gap:14px">
    
    <div class="card step-card is-first">
      <span class="step-no">1</span>
      <h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:7px">Account opening</h4>
      <p style="font-size:12px">Facility licence · commercial registration · VAT certificate · contact details.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card step-card">
      <span class="step-no">2</span>
      <h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:7px">Ordering</h4>
      <p style="font-size:12px">WhatsApp, email, or a rep visit — with an official, documented quote.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card step-card">
      <span class="step-no">3</span>
      <h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:7px">Delivery</h4>
      <p style="font-size:12px">A delivery note, the lot data, and a compliant tax invoice.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card step-card">
      <span class="step-no">4</span>
      <h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:7px">Training & practice</h4>
      <p style="font-size:12px">Hands-on training for the medical team, with free trial samples at first engagement.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card step-card">
      <span class="step-no">5</span>
      <h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:7px">Follow-up</h4>
      <p style="font-size:12px">Monitoring consumption and reordering on time so your work never stops.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="foot-note">Accounts open within 1–3 business days of complete documents, and your account manager follows up on reorders regularly before stock runs out.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section" id="terms"><div class="container">
  <div class="grid grid-2" style="gap:16px">
    <div class="card" style="padding:28px 30px">
      <h3 class="card__title" style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:16px">Commercial terms</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Payment methods: bank transfer · mada · Visa · cash on delivery.</li>
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Invoicing: a compliant tax invoice with every shipment, with the lot data attached.</li>
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Corporate accounts: credit terms are available for medical groups per agreement with the facility.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="padding:28px 30px">
      <h3 class="card__title" style="font-size:17px;margin-bottom:16px">Shelf-life & replacement policy</h3>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Shelf life at delivery: remaining validity of no less than 12 months from the date of receipt.</li>
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Damaged on arrival: any damaged unit is replaced when reported within 48 hours of receipt.</li>
        <li><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Near-expiry stock: replacement or return cases are coordinated with your account manager under an approved policy.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-top:16px"><div class="note-strip"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5-7-10V6z"></path><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"></path></svg><p>Any clause without an approved written policy is removed from the published version — an unconfirmed promise is riskier than its absence. And by meeting decision: no minimum order is stated.</p></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section--mint" id="training"><div class="container">
  
<div class="sec-head">
  <span class="eyebrow"><i></i>Training & technical support</span>
  <h2 class="sec-title">With every supply — approved protocols and support for the medical team</h2>
  
</div>
  <div class="grid grid-3">
    <div class="card" style="padding:24px"><h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:15px">Usage protocols</h4><p style="line-height:1.95">Documented guides to injection areas, recommended depths and suggested volumes per product — as issued by the manufacturer.</p></div><div class="card" style="padding:24px"><h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:15px">Visual training material</h4><p style="line-height:1.95">Educational media presented by practising physicians with direct product experience.</p></div><div class="card" style="padding:24px"><h4 class="card__title" style="font-size:15px">Technical assistance</h4><p style="line-height:1.95">Technical and explanatory support at the clinic’s first use, with follow-up for any later enquiry.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="foot-note">Training is delivered in person at the facility on first supply, supported by video material — with an attendance certificate for the hands-on session.</p>
</div></section>

